Subject: [PATCH] Select M64 expert row tiles for large native TP3 prefill

Upstream image base: vLLM19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354,
r6f image tree4127ff975d84320923471c9cad770a69aeec41f3.
Effective source base: accepted seven-overlay recipe9ff535dc68ddbf248f52c4eb41f4d6fccbbd9efa.
This delta applies to the accepted served adapter SHA256999c937450a1038b0de528335a74c56d33de0c0c2364d4263eeda5beb7657e2d,
NOT directly to an unmodified upstream vLLM checkout.
Result SHA256: 072d2a99d1cbdb538ce5fbba6c0ca66935f234bb9f9e33e0d2e9ded860e73526.

Rationale: improve the native384-expert/6-route/H5120/I768 prefill path at
rows>=2048. Keep M32 for smaller/other shapes, N128 weight packing once,
three pipeline stages, FP32 ordered combine and existing BF16 output fold.
Quality: same-input byte equality observed in1300 isolated replays and8100
actual model shadow comparisons; this is not a universal mathematical proof.
Capacity/memory qualification and final normal-cache layout remain pending.
Upstream status: owner's private fork change; no upstream submission planned.
Tests: existing wave7 native receipts; pending capacity receipts enumerated
in the accompanying qualification-gates.json. No sampling changes.

